                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h3] Less Pixelated and Better Level Ups [/h3]\n\nIn my opinion, the EX version is better than the first version of this game. \n\n[h3] The Big Gripe [/h3]\n\nBut you still have to actually land a Y attack on the boss with your thumbstick pointing at the boss before you get a \"lock on\" status. That status might randomly disappear on you, too. And trash mobs will be cheesing you from all over the place. Your enemies can easily get 50-hit combos where you just get tossed around without any ability to do anything about it. But if you can manage to get a \"lock on\" status and hit the boss during your \"burst,\" you have a chance of beating the powerful bosses in the game.\n\n[h3] The Small Gripes [/h3]\n\n1) In campaign mode, expect to find a mission you can quickly complete and then repeating that mission 30-50 times before you try to find the next mission like it further into the story.\n2) The Free Play missions are difficult to the point of being absurd at two out of five stars of difficulty. I honestly wonder how many fans of this game have cleared all of the Free Play missions.\n\n[h3] Suggestion [/h3]\n\nIf you are a fan boy wanting to spend time with Princess Solange, your best bet would be buying Blade Strangers. Look it up.",
